 "word_count": 151,
 "lines": [
  "They found his name hidden in the walls, written on lead among spells and human remains.",
  "The historian Tacitus says Germanicus was still alive when they were discovered.",
  "Germanicus was the emperor's adopted son, sent east with authority over Rome's governors.",
  "But Piso, the governor of Syria, overturned his orders.",
  "When Germanicus fell ill, he believed Piso had poisoned him.",
  "The hidden lead sheets were curses, meant to deliver him to the gods below.",
  "Before he died, Germanicus begged his friends to bring Piso to justice.",
  "So in Rome, Piso was put on trial before the Senate, accused of poisoning Germanicus.",
  "Before the verdict, Piso was found dead, a sword beside him.",
